WEBVTT

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:09.130
First Game

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.130
<i>The practice match with Mozuyama
enters the decider.</i>

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:13.050
<i>Koyori returns Futamaru Kururi's shot.</i>

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:14.320
<i>But...</i>

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:23.430
One-love.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.880
<i>I thought I hit that smash
toward her backhand,</i>

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:30.590
<i>but it swerved way left.</i>

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:34.220
<i>My stroke's trajectory
was knocked completely off kilter...</i>

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:38.180
<i>Almost like it hit some kind of wall.</i>

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:43.500
<i>One of the Elite Four Drivers,</i>

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:44.890
<i>the Driver of the East.</i>

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:49.360
<i>That's Futamaru-san,
and this is her curve drive!</i>

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:51.110
Too bad.

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:54.430
Your heart-racing ecstasy

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:58.030
will never reach

00:00:58.690 --> 00:00:59.950
me.

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:31.230
<b>Scorching</b>

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:31.230
<b>Ping Pong Girls</b>

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:11.970
Nobody can counter her curve drive.

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:14.110
<i>No matter what you do,
I'll be the one to win.</i>

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:15.990
<i>The ironclad tenet I live and die by!</i>

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.400
<i>All for Zakuro!</i>

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:47.810
<b>Tenth Serve</b>

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:47.810
<b>My Brand of Table Tennis</b>

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:48.770
Second Game

00:02:52.990 --> 00:02:54.190
Six-love.

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:02.340
No way.

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:04.830
Koyori-senpai's being dominated.

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:08.170
Oh, there it is again.

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:11.200
What is that weird stroke?

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:12.880
The curve drive.

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:18.090
It's a type of breaking drive
that curves dramatically to Koyori's right.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:21.800
And when you try to return it,
it tends to swerve to the left.

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:25.100
How does that happen?

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:26.510
It's friction at work.

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:31.350
The curve drive is a drive with both
top- and counter-clockwise spin.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:35.730
The ball uses the opponent's rubber
as a sort of springboard,

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:39.110
making it curve wildly to the left.

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:41.220
And...

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:45.030
The more spin applied,
the more it swerves.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:48.060
Normally, the curve drive is used

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:52.370
to gain the upper hand in rallies by forcing
the opponent toward their forehand.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:59.510
But Kururi-senpai's swing
imparts a massive amount of spin,

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:03.310
turning the stroke into a OHKO move.

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:11.390
Making her opponents feel
like they're hitting the ball at a tornado,

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:16.220
this is the ultimate move
of Futamaru Kururi, the Driver of the East.

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:20.860
Nobody can counter her curve drive.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.150
I-It can't be!

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:25.490
Don't tell me, Koyori-senpai...

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:31.330
Koyori-senpai's smash...

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:33.080
...isn't working at all!

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:36.220
Th-There's no way to beat someone like this!

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:38.040
Koyori-senpai!

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:42.260
<i>All the opponents I've overwhelmed
with this stroke</i>

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:45.090
<i>lost their will to fight.</i>

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:51.720
<i>I'm sure you're wearing
a look of despair, too.</i>

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:53.730
Amazing.

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:58.060
I've never seen a drive
that curves this sharply before.

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:05.240
My heart's racing!

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:06.920
<i>She's smiling?!</i>

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:09.700
But, if I keep getting destroyed like this,

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:13.050
your heart can't race, can it?

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:17.320
Now, it's my turn to make your heart race

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:19.340
with my brand of table tennis!

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:29.200
That's our Kururi-senpai!
You took a two game lead!

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:31.760
Keep going and win in straight games!

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.730
What's the matter, Kururi?

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:38.370
Something on your mind?

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:40.690
No, it's nothing.

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:44.410
Don't worry. I will win.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:45.650
I swear to death.

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:48.110
<i>For Zakuro.</i>

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:53.580
Incredible! Absolutely incredible!

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.280
It curves so much!

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:55.280
Incredible!

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:57.500
And my returns don't go straight!

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:00.380
Incredible! Her curve drive
is way too incredible!

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:02.610
This is no time to dance with joy!

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:03.810
What're you going to do?

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:05.930
You're two games behind!
Your back's against the wall!

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:08.760
And to top it off,
you can't return her curve drives at all!

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:10.040
Do you understand?!

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:11.520
Id hurdz!

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:15.350
I-It's not like I'm playing
without a plan, you know.

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:20.260
I'm not quite there yet,
but I do know a way to score off of her.

00:06:20.260 --> 00:06:21.070
Oh?

00:06:21.070 --> 00:06:23.130
Wow, that's awesome, Taily!

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:24.230
So you've got a chance, huh?

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:28.450
Looks like it's going to
come in handy already.

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:32.030
That thing we did where we groped
for the spot that felt the best.

00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:34.150
Groped for the spot that felt the best?

00:06:34.150 --> 00:06:35.410
They groped?

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:36.700
Senpai...

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:39.920
Wait, what? What's that all about?

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:41.170
W-Well...

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:44.210
My, what did you two get up to?

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:45.030
I-It's not...

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:47.320
I'd very much like to know.

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:49.930
I-It wasn't a big deal, really.

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:51.410
Feel good!

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:52.140
Tail! Tail!

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:55.250
Oh, come on! It was practice!

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:57.100
We practiced hitting the ball
off the sweet spot!

00:06:58.060 --> 00:06:59.600
Sweet spot?

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:01.860
You've heard of it in baseball, right?

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:03.840
Like, hitting a pitch
right off the meat of the bat.

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:07.650
Table tennis rackets have them, too.

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:12.530
Sweet spots where the ball jumps off faster,
even with the exact same swing.

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:17.670
If you can hit the ball
using this spot at will,

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:20.730
your smash will improve drastically.

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:29.050
Sweet spots are generally
toward the center and sound different.

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:30.010
Tail!

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:33.650
And, even though the hits feel light,
the ball just jumps off the bat.

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:38.350
Simply put, it's the spot
that makes your shots feel the best.

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:42.810
The sweet spot varies
depending on stroke and swing speed.

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:51.200
Anyway, just hit lots of balls
and drill that spot into your body.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:52.460
Okay!

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:58.840
Thinking about how it'll help me
hit better smashes is making my heart race.

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:00.410
Thanks, Agari-chan.

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:03.820
I-It's not a big deal, really!

00:08:03.820 --> 00:08:07.880
But why did you suddenly decide to coach me?

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:13.210
Hokuto replaced your rubber
with a more responsive one, right?

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:14.150
Yeah.

00:08:14.150 --> 00:08:18.310
That makes it easier
to look for the sweet spot,

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:20.850
so I figured now was the best time.

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:28.790
B-Besides, I brought back my forehand smash
and got better thanks to you.

00:08:28.790 --> 00:08:34.740
So I thought it'd be unfair if
I did nothing in return...

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:38.120
Did I do something for you?

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:41.940
Wh-Who cares?!

00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:43.460
Get back to practice!

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:45.010
Koyori, here!

00:08:45.010 --> 00:08:46.330
Here, here!

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:49.290
We will now start the third game.

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:50.840
I see.

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:52.820
Third Game

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:55.760
So all those errant smashes so far
were her trying to find the sweet spot?

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:57.970
Looks like it.

00:08:58.310 --> 00:08:59.230
But, you know,

00:08:59.230 --> 00:09:04.150
what does this sweet spot have to do
with countering the curve drive?

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:07.360
Strokes hit off the sweet spot are faster,

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:09.730
so she must be trying to use that speed.

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:10.930
Yeah.

00:09:18.980 --> 00:09:20.580
<i>That one felt good.</i>

00:09:21.140 --> 00:09:23.490
<i>But it wasn't enough.</i>

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:25.830
<i>I should be able to feel even better.</i>

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:30.040
<i>Unlike in practice,</i>

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:33.660
<i>the curve made it hard
to hit the ball right in the middle,</i>

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:35.720
<i>but I'm finally getting the hang of it.</i>

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:37.430
<i>I'll nail it this time.</i>

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:39.660
<i>Pointless.</i>

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:42.390
<i>No matter what you do,
I'll be the one to win.</i>

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:46.390
<i>Every time I won, Zakuro smiled for me.</i>

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:48.100
<i>The friendship fee...</i>

00:09:48.490 --> 00:09:52.570
<i>Tending to her and giving her presents
is just a bonus.</i>

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:55.290
<i>More than any other gift,</i>

00:09:55.290 --> 00:09:59.260
<i>she shows me the greatest smile
when I win in table tennis.</i>

00:09:59.940 --> 00:10:02.330
<i>To see that smile,</i>

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:08.660
<i>I will win!</i>

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:11.790
<i>Gifting her victory</i>

00:10:13.070 --> 00:10:15.460
<i>is the ironclad tenet I live and die by!</i>

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:20.730
<i>All for Zakuro!</i>

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:24.140
Kururi! Behind you!

00:10:26.710 --> 00:10:27.790
<i>There it is!</i>

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:30.060
<i>Right at the spot
that feels the absolute best!</i>

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:32.060
<i>And now, the smash!</i>

00:10:42.340 --> 00:10:44.990
That felt <i>so</i> good!

00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:47.610
Koyori-senpai did it...

00:10:47.610 --> 00:10:49.750
She beat the curve drive!

00:10:52.140 --> 00:10:53.540
I'm so glad.

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:55.450
At last...

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:59.970
At last, you looked my way.

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:15.280
<i>My curve drive was broken down?</i>

00:11:16.580 --> 00:11:19.400
<i>No! Not even in death!</i>

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:20.530
<i>It can't be!</i>

00:11:22.420 --> 00:11:24.240
<i>It has to be a fluke!</i>

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:30.620
Peach Panties returned curve drives
in quick succession.

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:32.110
Say, Agari.

00:11:32.110 --> 00:11:35.200
Is this the result of all your groping?

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:38.710
Yeah. She used the sweet spot
to brute force the curve drive.

00:11:39.490 --> 00:11:42.490
It was swerving her shots way left

00:11:42.490 --> 00:11:44.150
and, like there was a wall in the way,

00:11:44.150 --> 00:11:47.340
she couldn't make her shots land
in the other half of the court.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:52.730
But she used the extra speed
from the sweet spot to force it in.

00:11:53.290 --> 00:11:56.340
Since the ball jumps
off the sweet spot faster,

00:11:56.340 --> 00:11:59.750
it's less susceptible to spin and,
consequently, curve.

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:01.120
Ah!

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:04.030
There are several ways
to counter the curve drive,

00:12:05.770 --> 00:12:09.540
but, given Koyori-chan's love for smashes,
this method is very her.

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:11.750
<i>This can't be.</i>

00:12:14.930 --> 00:12:17.040
<i>My curve drive is losing?</i>

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:19.760
<i>Our curve drive?</i>

00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:27.310
Sometimes, your drives
curve to the left, don't they?

00:12:27.950 --> 00:12:29.570
It's a bad habit of mine.

00:12:29.570 --> 00:12:31.980
Curving it deliberately would be one thing,

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:35.970
but it's not good that the ball curves
even when I hit it normally.

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:40.860
Then, hey, let's turn it into an asset!

00:12:41.180 --> 00:12:45.640
I mean, there's a stroke
called the curve drive, right?

00:12:45.640 --> 00:12:47.480
Make it your own!

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:50.100
Uh, you see,

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:53.460
I'm always holding you back during practice,

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:57.830
so I want to do something 
that helps you, too.

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:05.760
<i>This stroke I developed
with Zakuro will lose?</i>

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:13.260
<i>No... Anything but that.</i>

00:13:13.260 --> 00:13:14.270
<i>I'd rather face death!</i>

00:13:18.630 --> 00:13:21.320
<i>She used a backhand drive
on a perfect chance for a curve drive?!</i>

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:23.570
Yay!

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:26.660
Taily took the third game!

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:32.580
Fourth Game

00:13:38.590 --> 00:13:41.880
Koyori's had all the momentum
since she conquered the curve drive.

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:43.510
She can take this all the way!

00:13:43.910 --> 00:13:46.930
No way. Kururi-senpai's on the back foot.

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:49.340
I've never seen her get cornered like this.

00:13:49.940 --> 00:13:52.810
She's not using the curve drive at all.

00:13:54.780 --> 00:13:57.310
I love the way you play
table tennis, Futamaru-san!

00:13:57.720 --> 00:14:00.770
<i>I'm supposed to be Zakuro's ideal!</i>

00:14:01.370 --> 00:14:03.820
<i>If I don't win, Zakuro won't smile for me!</i>

00:14:04.620 --> 00:14:07.240
<i>She won't stay by my side!</i>

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:10.460
Eleven-six.

00:14:10.460 --> 00:14:12.280
Game to Tsumujikaze.

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:18.950
<i>I'm going to lose?</i>

00:14:20.270 --> 00:14:22.860
<i>Am I going to lose?</i>

00:14:24.030 --> 00:14:25.400
<i>That won't do.</i>

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:26.790
<i>I have to win.</i>

00:14:26.790 --> 00:14:29.090
<i>I'll be worthless if I don't win.</i>

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:32.550
<i>Zakuro will leave me!</i>

00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:34.420
<i>Win...</i>

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:36.910
<i>Win, win, win...</i>

00:14:36.910 --> 00:14:39.440
<i>Win, win, win, win!</i>

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:40.100
Kururi!

00:14:48.730 --> 00:14:51.330
Tsumujikaze-san is
an amazing player, isn't she?

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:55.710
Hellbent on returning your curve drives,

00:14:55.710 --> 00:14:57.620
she hit, and hit, and hit...

00:14:57.970 --> 00:15:00.540
She came directly at you
with sheer unyielding will.

00:15:04.580 --> 00:15:05.810
Don't worry.

00:15:06.350 --> 00:15:09.450
Win or lose, it won't change who you are.

00:15:10.870 --> 00:15:14.390
So stick to your brand of 
table tennis all the way.

00:15:18.090 --> 00:15:21.690
The brand of tennis I love so much.

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:26.520
<i>My brand of table tennis...?</i>

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:32.490
Fifth Game

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:34.460
<i>This is it.</i>

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:36.200
<i>Winner takes all.</i>

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:42.920
Love-all!

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:50.020
She brought out the curve drive again?

00:15:50.020 --> 00:15:51.740
But it was out.

00:15:51.740 --> 00:15:52.840
By a mile.

00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:07.240
Yeah, she's completely lost it!

00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:08.850
I wouldn't be so sure.

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:14.780
<i>She's playing just like Koyori
in the early going!</i>

00:16:15.090 --> 00:16:17.510
What's gotten into Kururi-senpai?

00:16:17.510 --> 00:16:19.340
She broke, nom.

00:16:19.340 --> 00:16:21.630
<i>No. She's taking a gamble.</i>

00:16:21.630 --> 00:16:25.250
<i>In these closing stages, she's trying
to make her curve drive evolve.</i>

00:16:27.470 --> 00:16:30.450
<i>She's putting her very soul
into every last hit.</i>

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:31.920
<i>Kururi!</i>

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:33.680
Five-eight.

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:35.390
<i>Tsumujikaze-san...</i>

00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:37.350
Five-nine.

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:39.010
<i>Tsumujikaze-san!</i>

00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:44.180
<i>You came directly at me
with your barrage of full-power smashes.</i>

00:16:44.180 --> 00:16:45.560
<i>A daring brand of table tennis!</i>

00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:47.690
Ten-five!

00:16:50.600 --> 00:16:52.960
<i>Then my brand of table tennis...</i>

00:16:54.710 --> 00:16:56.520
<i>My brand of table tennis is...</i>

00:17:00.810 --> 00:17:01.450
Don't tell me!

00:17:01.840 --> 00:17:02.410
Senpai?!

00:17:02.890 --> 00:17:03.500
Kururi!

00:17:07.220 --> 00:17:09.920
<i>...using this stroke I developed with Zakuro,</i>

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:12.500
<i>this stroke I love so much,</i>

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:18.450
<i>to fight to the death!</i>

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:25.860
<i>Is she trying to force it in by changing
the initial direction of her shot?!</i>

00:17:25.860 --> 00:17:28.980
<i>A curve drive that wouldn't land inside
unless she did...</i>

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:30.360
Kururi-senpai!

00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:31.360
Kururi!

00:17:31.770 --> 00:17:33.340
<i>Tsumujikaze-san,</i>

00:17:33.340 --> 00:17:38.110
<i>how will you respond to my racing heart?</i>

00:17:44.980 --> 00:17:47.540
<i>This is Futamaru-san's brand of table tennis!</i>

00:17:48.220 --> 00:17:52.550
<i>I want to respond in kind,
with every fiber of my being!</i>

00:17:55.670 --> 00:17:58.340
<i>Direct all the power I have forward!</i>

00:17:58.810 --> 00:17:59.830
Tsumujikaze-san!

00:17:59.830 --> 00:18:00.550
Koyori!

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:02.060
Get in!

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:04.310
Get in there!

00:18:07.410 --> 00:18:09.350
Go, my brand of table tennis!

00:18:09.740 --> 00:18:11.310
Go, my racing, scorching heart!

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:15.320
Reach her!

00:18:27.060 --> 00:18:29.020
E-Eleven-six!

00:18:29.020 --> 00:18:31.890
Game and match to Tsumujikaze!

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:36.210
Koyori!

00:18:36.620 --> 00:18:37.470
Kururi!

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:41.830
Are you okay, Koyori?!

00:18:41.830 --> 00:18:42.730
Yeah...

00:18:42.730 --> 00:18:44.170
Really? Are you really okay?

00:18:44.170 --> 00:18:46.090
I-I'm fine.

00:18:46.090 --> 00:18:49.380
Sheesh, how could you play until you dropped?

00:18:49.380 --> 00:18:50.910
You push yourself too much.

00:18:53.120 --> 00:18:58.030
But, well, I guess that's
why you conquered that curve drive.

00:19:00.770 --> 00:19:03.450
That made my heart race
incredibly fast, Koyori!

00:19:06.050 --> 00:19:08.260
That was awesome, Taily!

00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:09.320
Nice play.

00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:12.750
D-Don't taily me right now!

00:19:13.890 --> 00:19:15.460
I'm sorry.

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:17.210
I lost.

00:19:17.730 --> 00:19:19.920
I played an ugly game.

00:19:23.320 --> 00:19:24.850
That's not true.

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:31.020
It was a great game, Kururi.

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:33.330
Wh-What are you saying...

00:19:34.240 --> 00:19:37.530
But I lost...

00:19:38.040 --> 00:19:41.330
That seriously fired me up, Senpai!

00:19:41.330 --> 00:19:42.730
It was inspiring.

00:19:42.730 --> 00:19:43.900
Kururi-senpai!

00:19:43.900 --> 00:19:44.990
Nom, nom!

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:48.300
I...

00:19:51.770 --> 00:19:52.920
<i>I...</i>

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:56.390
<i>I was mistaken, after all.</i>

00:20:01.350 --> 00:20:06.080
<i>I never needed to pay a friendship fee.</i>

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:20.900
<b>Suzumegahara vs. Mozuyama</b>

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:20.900
<b>Tenka Hanabi 2   3 Sasorida Sachiko</b>

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:20.900
<b>Itsumo Hokuto 2   3 Yuragi Yura</b>

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:20.900
<b>Ushirode Kiruka 3   1 Kanenashi Mayuu</b>

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:20.900
<b>Munemune                Hamu Kimiko</b>

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:20.900
<b>Kamiya Agari 3   2 Zashikiwarashi Zakuro</b>

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:20.900
<b>Tsumujikaze Koyori 3   2 Futamaru Kururi</b>

00:20:09.570 --> 00:20:14.500
And so, the match
between Suzumegahara and Mozuyama

00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:18.720
ended in a 3-2 victory for Suzumegahara.

00:20:22.060 --> 00:20:24.240
Thank you very much!

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:29.200
I won't lose next time, Sasorin!

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:31.160
S-Sasorin?

00:20:31.850 --> 00:20:32.870
Fere.

00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:34.440
Beam, beam.

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:35.830
Th-Thanks.

00:20:37.430 --> 00:20:40.430
Thank you so much for coming all this way!

00:20:40.430 --> 00:20:42.590
Oh, no, the pleasure was all ours.

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:48.060
K-Kamiya-san!

00:20:49.570 --> 00:20:52.480
Thank oo for agarieat game!

00:20:54.190 --> 00:20:55.400
Sure.

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:58.130
Sway, sway.

00:21:02.140 --> 00:21:04.280
The world is full of mysteries.

00:21:09.890 --> 00:21:15.870
Your shots told me just how much
you love the curve drive.

00:21:17.440 --> 00:21:22.130
It made me really happy
that you came at me with all that love!

00:21:24.460 --> 00:21:25.840
It's strange.

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:30.060
"Forget winning or losing,
I want to bare everything I have right now."

00:21:30.630 --> 00:21:34.180
"I want to see how she will respond
when I go all-out."

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:37.080
That's how you made me feel.

00:21:41.740 --> 00:21:45.110
Playing table tennis with you
made my heart race.

00:21:50.980 --> 00:21:52.080
Same here!

00:21:55.410 --> 00:22:01.500
Next time, we'll be stronger,
and we'll make your hearts race even more,

00:22:02.160 --> 00:22:04.170
so you'd best be prepared.

00:22:05.680 --> 00:22:06.630
Yes!

00:22:09.120 --> 00:22:13.810
Let's feel our hearts race even more,
in the tournament this time!

00:23:43.770 --> 00:24:00.000
Preview

00:23:44.830 --> 00:23:47.840
We'll train hard to prepare
for the tournament!

00:23:47.190 --> 00:23:48.440
Was that directed at me?

00:23:47.840 --> 00:23:50.280
So this is a training camp...

00:23:49.070 --> 00:23:50.280
I think I might die.

00:23:50.280 --> 00:23:51.650
Smash practice?!

00:23:50.720 --> 00:23:52.620
Hot spring!

00:23:51.650 --> 00:23:53.610
One of these items isn't like the others...

00:23:53.610 --> 00:23:55.420
I-If you're okay with me...

00:23:54.300 --> 00:23:56.450
Did you soak to your shoulders
and count one hundred?

00:23:55.420 --> 00:23:57.740
You sound like an old woman, White Panties.
